<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Epi.Rendering</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    Rendering reads content and nothing else: no lifecycle, and no ambient clock. A render is a
    pure function of a label version and a render-template version (ADR-033 decision 1).

    This comment used to say "no store, no clock" and mean the whole project. That stopped being
    true when the asset store landed here, and object-lock retention needs a deadline. The rule
    that carries the weight is narrower and still holds: nothing in this project reads the clock
    for itself. The store is handed a TimeProvider, and neither renderer can reach it, so a
    render still cannot embed the moment it was made.

    The asset store's presence here is a boundary worth revisiting - ingesting artwork is not
    rendering, and it is only here because rendering was what needed it first (recorded as a
    debt in design/iteration-3.md).
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Epi.ContentCore\Epi.ContentCore.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- The AWS SDK is Apache-2.0. It is here for the S3 API rather than for AWS: the object
       store is MinIO (ADR-013), and anything else speaking S3 would serve as well, which is
       what makes ADR-034 decision 4 more than a claim. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="AWSSDK.S3" Version="3.7.415.9" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
